    },
    {
      "start": 88.0,
      "end": 94.0,
      "text": "This is life's support for the air inside my chest"
    },
    {
      "start": 94.0,
      "end": 101.0,
      "text": "I'm not escaping, not arrival, just a way to keep it fresh"
    },
    {
      "start": 101.0,
      "end": 108.0,
      "text": "I have laid a breathing garden from the phases I survived"
    },
    {
      "start": 108.0,
      "end": 114.0,
      "text": "Every song becomes a chamber within a weather thrive"
    },
    {
      "start": 114.0,
      "end": 128.0,
      "text": "I used to call creation proof, something bright enough to show"
    },
    {
      "start": 128.0,
      "end": 138.0,
      "text": "Now I know it as a climate, something tended so I grow there are days that glass feels heavy"
    },
    {
      "start": 138.0,
      "end": 145.0,
      "text": "Days the orbit pulls me thin, then I hear the roots feel"
    },
    {
      "start": 145.0,
      "end": 157.0,
      "text": "Moving patiently within no grand end, no closed gate"
    },
    {
      "start": 158.0,
      "end": 167.0,
      "text": "A life is not a straight line, it is circulation"
    },
    {
      "start": 167.0,
      "end": 175.0,
      "text": "A song is not a trophy, it is atmosphere"
    },
    {
